<div style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; border: 1px solid #ddd;">

    <h1 style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; margin-top: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 2</h1>
    <p style="text-align: center; font-style: italic; margin-bottom: 20px;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>

    <h2 style="color: #1a5276; border-bottom: 2px solid #1a5276; padding-bottom: 5px;">SECTION 2 — LESSON IDENTIFICATION TABLE</h2>
    <table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 2</td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Reading</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 9th Grade (CEFR: A2.4)</td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Renewable Energy in Panama</td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Why Is Renewable Energy Important for Panama?</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Reading: Reading: Interpret written instructions for daily activities. Reading: Recognize the language on a simple form asking for personal information.</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Reading: Can interpret instructions on saving energy in daily routines (e.g., "To save energy, you should turn off the TV when you're not watching, and unplug chargers when they're not in use.")
Can identify and fill in the required information in surveys and forms related to renewable energy in Panama (e.g., "Indicate if your home uses solar panels," "yes or no," or "Check whether your home uses LED bulbs or traditional bulbs.")
Can interpret steps in a guide on setting up home energy-saving habits (e.g., "Summertime instructions on how to unplug devices at school and reduce fan or A/C use during the day.").</p>
                </td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 style="color: #1a5276; border-bottom: 2px solid #1a5276; padding-bottom: 5px; margin-top: 30px;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
    <table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
                <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 33%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
                <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 33%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays a short "Energy Habits Quiz" with 3-4 True/False statements (e.g., "Turning off lights when you leave a room saves energy." "Using a fan instead of AC always consumes more electricity."). Students read each statement and show a "T" or "F" card to indicate their answer. This activates prior knowledge about energy conservation.</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models how to read instructions carefully by showing a simple instruction (e.g., "Unplug your phone charger when not in use.") on the board. The teacher reads it aloud, emphasizing the verbs and key nouns, and models the stress in words like "unplug," "charger," and "energy." They then demonstrate how to quickly skim for the main idea. "Remember, saving energy is important because it preserves natural resources."</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b>
                    <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When we read instructions, are we looking for general information or specific steps?" (Specific steps)</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If a text mentions 'unplugging devices,' what action should we think about?" (Removing plugs from electrical outlets)</li>
                    </ul></p>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Renewable Energy in Panama")</p>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> The teacher provides students with a handout containing two short texts:
                    <ol style="margin-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">A "Panama Energy-Saving Tips" guide with 4-5 numbered instructions for daily routines (e.g., "To save energy, you should turn off the TV when you're not watching, and unplug chargers when they're not in use.").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">A "Home Renewable Energy Survey" form asking for basic personal information and yes/no questions about home energy use (e.g., "Indicate if your home uses solar panels: Yes/No," "Check whether your home uses LED bulbs or traditional bulbs.").</li>
                    </ol>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">These texts integrate vocabulary like <i>energy, solar, electricity, consumption, save, unplug, LED, efficient</i>, and grammar like gerunds ("Saving energy is important...") and present continuous ("Many homes are switching to LED bulbs.").</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Genre, Register, Format:</b> Instructional guide, simple survey form. Informational, semi-formal. Printed text handout.</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Comprehends short, clear written instructions and simple forms related to daily activities and personal information, recognizing key vocabulary and grammatical structures.</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b>
                    <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist questions:</b> Students read both texts quickly and answer: "What is the main goal of the 'Energy-Saving Tips' guide?" and "What kind of information does the 'Home Renewable Energy Survey' ask for?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Students read specific statements about the texts and mark them as True or False (e.g., "The guide suggests leaving lights on when you leave a room." - False. "The survey asks if your home uses wind turbines." - Depends on the actual survey, but for A2.4 keep it simple, e.g., "The survey asks about solar panels." - True).</li>
                    </ul></p>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Reading)</p>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Reading comprehension, identifying target vocabulary (e.g., <i>conservation, efficiency, panels, consumption, preserve, generate</i>), and understanding grammar (gerunds for actions, present continuous for ongoing actions, adverbial clauses for justification like <i>because, since</i>).</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                    <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice (Gap-fill/Matching):</b> Students read sentences extracted from the texts or new sentences related to the theme, with blanks for target vocabulary words or grammatical structures. For instance, "_____ energy is important for the future." (Saving). "We are currently _____ more efficient technology." (installing/implementing). They choose words from a box. Or, students match definitions to key vocabulary from the text (e.g., "turbine" with "a machine that generates electricity").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice (Sentence Completion with Justification):</b> The teacher provides sentence beginnings related to energy saving or renewable energy, and students complete them by reading provided options or their own ideas, focusing on adverbial clauses for justification. E.g., "You should turn off the lights _____" (because it reduces electricity consumption / since it saves money). "Renewable energy is beneficial for Panama _____" (as it preserves natural resources / due to its sustainability).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Check and Correction:</b> In pairs, students read their completed sentences and gap-fills to each other, comparing answers with the original texts and discussing any discrepancies. They practice reading the target vocabulary and grammatically correct sentences. The teacher circulates, monitoring for accuracy and providing support.</li>
                    </ul></p>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">12-15 min</p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Renewable Energy in Panama")</p>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Students will individually read and complete an "Energy-Saving Home Audit & Commitment Form." This form will include:
                    <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">A section with instructions on how to conduct a simple energy audit at home (e.g., "Summertime instructions on how to unplug devices at school and reduce fan or A/C use during the day.").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Questions where students must read and check boxes or fill in short answers based on their home's energy consumption and potential for saving (e.g., "Do you regularly unplug chargers? Yes/No/Sometimes," "List two devices you could unplug more often.").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">A commitment section where they interpret and select 2-3 energy-saving actions they pledge to implement, justifying why they chose them (e.g., "I will turn off lights more because it's easy and saves electricity.").</li>
                    </ul></p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to Theme/Scenario:</b> The task directly applies the learned vocabulary and reading skills to a personal, actionable scenario related to energy saving in Panama, emphasizing the importance of individual contribution to sustainability. Students are reading practical instructions and questions to analyze their own energy consumption and justify their choices.</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Reading comprehension for practical application, identifying required information, and interpreting instructions accurately to complete a task. Using target grammar (gerunds, adverbial clauses) and vocabulary in a meaningful context.</p>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist during the "Performance" stage, focusing on students' ability to interpret and complete the form. Collection and review of the "Energy-Saving Home Audit & Commitment Form."</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students submit their completed "Energy-Saving Home Audit & Commitment Form." The teacher checks for accuracy in interpreting instructions, relevance of the information provided, and the correct use of target vocabulary and grammar.</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
                    <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Ability to interpret written instructions for daily activities (e.g., how to conduct the audit).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accuracy in recognizing and filling in required personal and energy-related information on the form.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of target vocabulary (<i>energy, consumption, save, unplug, efficient</i>) when completing the form.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of gerunds and adverbial clauses for justification in the commitment section (e.g., "Saving energy is important because...").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and completeness of the form entries.</li>
                    </ul></p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer the following questions on a small slip of paper:
                    <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was the most challenging part of reading and completing the energy form today?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Name one new instruction you learned about saving energy."</li>
                    </ul></p>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b>
                    <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How confident do you feel now about interpreting instructions to save energy at home?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of the reading activities helped you understand the importance of renewable energy for Panama the most?"</li>
                    </ul></p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b>
                    <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in helping students interpret instructions and forms related to renewable energy? The explicit modeling and step-by-step practice for form completion seemed effective.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for next time? Perhaps providing a glossary of key terms for some students, or more visual aids for specific instructions, particularly for words like 'consumption' or 'infrastructure'. Some students struggled with differentiating between 'because' and 'since'.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The reading tasks effectively integrated vocabulary like 'sustainable,' 'efficient,' and 'preserve.' The pronunciation focus on 'renewable' and 'preservation' during modeling was also beneficial.</li>
                    </ul></p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> This lesson focused on reading about energy-saving and renewable energy. In Lesson 3, students will actively speak and interact using this vocabulary and grammatical structures, discussing the importance of these actions and justifying their opinions on Panama's energy future, building upon the information they read and interpreted today.</p>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">3-5 min</p>
                </td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>